@include ../../shared/squash.overtone

## Backhand length when tired
@track Out of 10
Backhand length when tired, four minutes. Behind the short line, straight drives aimed a racket head
above the service line, as earlier. Tired is when length drops short in a match, so hold the same
shot, resetting with a softer one whenever you need to. Halfway, go to the T between shots. In the
last thirty seconds, score ten by how many bounce first behind the short line.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 4:00
0:00 [go]
8% Aim higher, not harder.
25% Racket up early. Finish high.
50% Now drive, touch the T, and get back behind the next one.
65% Higher and softer whenever you need to reset.
80% Tired now. Hold the same shot.
-0:30 Ladder check. From behind the short line, score the next ten.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]
